window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b132-87c62d66b2cdf048.json"]={sha256:"87c62d66b2cdf04897296996e722f51e821f144ecde535878491b327796ad241",value:{"id":"b132","title":"隧道地表沉陷監測","titleEn":"Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦以基準穩定、沉陷槽形與時間關聯區分開挖及地下水影響。沿著調查依據、物理作用、數量估算、現場驗證到工程交接逐項建立可追溯的推論鏈，特別辨別單一數值無法揭露的空間差異及時間效應。以獨立量測檢驗簡化模型，並把觀測結果、教學假設與需要主管工程師審查的決策清楚分列。","summaryEn":"This course focuses on separate excavation and groundwater effects using stable benchmarks, trough geometry and time correlation. It develops a traceable reasoning chain from evidence and physical processes through quantitative estimates, field verification and engineering handover. Spatial variation and time effects are separated from a single nominal result. Independent observations test the simplified models, while measured evidence, teaching assumptions and decisions requiring the responsible engineer remain explicitly distinguished.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-investigation","subcategoryTitle":"地質調查與變形監測","subcategoryTitleEn":"Ground investigation and deformation monitoring","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-investigation","learningTags":["underground","ug-investigation","survey"],"architectureFamily":"survey","architectureNodes":[["沉陷槽形與參數","Settlement-trough geometry"],["穩定基準與閉合","Stable benchmarks and closure"],["速率與時間窗","Rates and time windows"],["地下水下降與固結","Drawdown and consolidation"],["長期追蹤與結案","Long-term tracking and closeout"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[3,1]],"diagram":{"type":"survey","labels":["沉陷槽形與參數","穩定基準與閉合","速率與時間窗","地下水下降與固結","長期追蹤與結案"],"labelsEn":["Settlement-trough geometry","Stable benchmarks and closure","Rates and time windows","Drawdown and consolidation","Long-term tracking and closeout"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創教學算例，所有輸入是為比較機制而假設，並非任何地標的實測資料。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=10 mm、i=5 m，x=5 m處S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm；假設沉陷向下為正。以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=0.01 m、i=5 m，Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m²；直徑6 m面積28.274 m²，VL=0.443%。將第一式的一個線性乘數加倍而固定其他邊界，該項貢獻隨之加倍；若為非線性式則必須重新代入，不能等比例外推。把輸入值、單位換算、計算結果及假設列成四欄，再用獨立計算器重算；最後比較量測誤差與模型簡化，判斷改變是否足以支持工程決策。","textEn":"Original teaching example: all inputs are assumptions for comparing mechanisms, not measurements from a landmark project. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=10 mm and i=5 m; at x=5 m, S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm, taking downward settlement as positive. The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=0.01 m and i=5 m; Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m². A 6 m diameter gives area 28.274 m² and VL=0.443%. Doubling one linear multiplicative input in the first relation while holding the remaining boundaries fixed doubles that contribution; a nonlinear relation must instead be evaluated again. Tabulate inputs, unit conversions, results and assumptions in separate columns, and recalculate independently. Finally compare measurement uncertainty with model simplification before deciding whether the difference supports an engineering decision.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b132-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「沉陷槽形與參數」與「體積損失換算」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Settlement-trough geometry\" and \"Volume-loss conversion\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b132-v14-01","title":"沉陷槽形與參數：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Settlement-trough geometry: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「沉陷槽形與參數」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Settlement-trough geometry” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"高斯沉陷槽用最大沉陷和寬度概括橫向地表變形，適合初步描述卻未必適合淺覆土、分層或強烈建物約束。斷面不足時兩參數互相補償，應以完整測點而非只看中線峰值。 假設Smax=10 mm、i=5 m，x=5 m處S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm；假設沉陷向下為正。 用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉陷槽形與參數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A Gaussian trough summarizes transverse movement with peak settlement and width, but shallow cover, layering and structural restraint can violate it. Sparse observations allow parameters to compensate for each other, requiring a full profile rather than only the centerline. Assume Smax=10 mm and i=5 m; at x=5 m, S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm, taking downward settlement as positive. Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Settlement-trough geometry” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉陷槽形與參數」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Settlement-trough geometry”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-01-k1","title":"沉陷槽形與參數","titleEn":"Settlement-trough geometry","text":"高斯沉陷槽用最大沉陷和寬度概括橫向地表變形，適合初步描述卻未必適合淺覆土、分層或強烈建物約束。斷面不足時兩參數互相補償，應以完整測點而非只看中線峰值。","textEn":"A Gaussian trough summarizes transverse movement with peak settlement and width, but shallow cover, layering and structural restraint can violate it. Sparse observations allow parameters to compensate for each other, requiring a full profile rather than only the centerline.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉陷槽形與參數」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Settlement-trough geometry\" is correct?","options":["量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。","高斯沉陷槽用最大沉陷和寬度概括橫向地表變形，適合初步描述卻未必適合淺覆土、分層或強烈建物約束。","地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。"],"optionsEn":["The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width.","A Gaussian trough summarizes transverse movement with peak settlement and width, but shallow cover, layering and structural restraint can violate it.","Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"高斯沉陷槽用最大沉陷和寬度概括橫向地表變形，適合初步描述卻未必適合淺覆土、分層或強烈建物約束。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A Gaussian trough summarizes transverse movement with peak settlement and width, but shallow cover, layering and structural restraint can violate it. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b132-v14-02","title":"沉陷槽形與參數：定量估算","titleEn":"Settlement-trough geometry: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉陷槽形與參數」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Settlement-trough geometry” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=10 mm、i=5 m，x=5 m處S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm；假設沉陷向下為正。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=10 mm and i=5 m; at x=5 m, S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm, taking downward settlement as positive. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=10 mm、i=5 m，x=5 m處S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm；假設沉陷向下為正。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=10 mm and i=5 m; at x=5 m, S=10e⁻⁰·⁵=6.07 mm, taking downward settlement as positive.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉陷槽形與參數」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Settlement-trough geometry\", which statement holds?","options":["建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。","儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage.","An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b132-v14-03","title":"沉陷槽形與參數：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Settlement-trough geometry: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉陷槽形與參數」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Settlement-trough geometry” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄沉陷槽形與參數的資料來源與適用條件。以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for settlement-trough geometry. Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved.","failure":"注意干擾：用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。","textEn":"Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄沉陷槽形與參數的資料來源與適用條件。以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for settlement-trough geometry. Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉陷槽形與參數」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Settlement-trough geometry\"?","options":["以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。"],"optionsEn":["Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一時間窗的橫斷面測點擬合並檢查殘差是否偏向一側，與地層及建物分布對照；量測涵蓋槽外穩定點，未覆蓋兩翼的斷面不得宣稱已可靠辨識槽寬。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fit points from one time window and inspect asymmetric residuals against geology and buildings; include stable points outside the trough and do not claim reliable width identification when both flanks are unobserved. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b132-v14-04","title":"沉陷槽形與參數：失效診斷","titleEn":"Settlement-trough geometry: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉陷槽形與參數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Settlement-trough geometry” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。","textEn":"Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. A fitted curve can pass through the available data yet misrepresent the influence zone and underestimate differential building movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉陷槽形與參數」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Settlement-trough geometry\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。","地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes.","Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用單點峰值推算整個沉陷槽會漏掉偏斜與多峰，擬合曲線可能穿過資料卻錯估影響範圍；鄰近建物的差異沉陷便被低估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Inferring the entire trough from one peak misses skew and multiple lobes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b132-v14-05","title":"體積損失換算：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Volume-loss conversion: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「體積損失換算」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Volume-loss conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"地表沉陷面積代表每單位隧道長度的地表體積變化，與開挖面積比得到表觀體積損失。排水固結、隆起與橫向位移會改變對應關係，不能把它視為直接秤出的超挖土量。 假設Smax=0.01 m、i=5 m，Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m²；直徑6 m面積28.274 m²，VL=0.443%。 把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「體積損失換算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Surface settlement area gives volume change per unit tunnel length, and its ratio to excavation area is apparent volume loss. Consolidation, heave and lateral movement alter the correspondence, so it is not directly weighed overexcavated soil. Assume Smax=0.01 m and i=5 m; Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m². A 6 m diameter gives area 28.274 m² and VL=0.443%. Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Volume-loss conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「體積損失換算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Volume-loss conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-05-k1","title":"體積損失換算","titleEn":"Volume-loss conversion","text":"地表沉陷面積代表每單位隧道長度的地表體積變化，與開挖面積比得到表觀體積損失。排水固結、隆起與橫向位移會改變對應關係，不能把它視為直接秤出的超挖土量。","textEn":"Surface settlement area gives volume change per unit tunnel length, and its ratio to excavation area is apparent volume loss. Consolidation, heave and lateral movement alter the correspondence, so it is not directly weighed overexcavated soil.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「體積損失換算」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Volume-loss conversion\" is correct?","options":["地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。","水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。","地表沉陷面積代表每單位隧道長度的地表體積變化，與開挖面積比得到表觀體積損失。"],"optionsEn":["Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage.","A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.","Surface settlement area gives volume change per unit tunnel length, and its ratio to excavation area is apparent volume loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"地表沉陷面積代表每單位隧道長度的地表體積變化，與開挖面積比得到表觀體積損失。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Surface settlement area gives volume change per unit tunnel length, and its ratio to excavation area is apparent volume loss. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b132-v14-06","title":"體積損失換算：定量估算","titleEn":"Volume-loss conversion: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「體積損失換算」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Volume-loss conversion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=0.01 m、i=5 m，Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m²；直徑6 m面積28.274 m²，VL=0.443%。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=0.01 m and i=5 m; Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m². A 6 m diameter gives area 28.274 m² and VL=0.443%. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設Smax=0.01 m、i=5 m，Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m²；直徑6 m面積28.274 m²，VL=0.443%。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume Smax=0.01 m and i=5 m; Vs=√(2π)iSmax=0.1253 m². A 6 m diameter gives area 28.274 m² and VL=0.443%.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「體積損失換算」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Volume-loss conversion\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。","水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning.","Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b132-v14-07","title":"體積損失換算：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Volume-loss conversion: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「體積損失換算」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Volume-loss conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄體積損失換算的資料來源與適用條件。以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for volume-loss conversion. Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen.","failure":"注意干擾：把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。","textEn":"Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄體積損失換算的資料來源與適用條件。以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for volume-loss conversion. Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「體積損失換算」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Volume-loss conversion\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。","大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter.","Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以量測斷面數值積分和高斯積分互相核對，統一沉陷單位與開挖直徑；比較施工後不同時段的面積變化，若有地下水降低，將延時固結與即時開挖損失分別討論。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Cross-check numerical profile integration against the Gaussian integral with consistent units and excavation diameter; compare later epochs and distinguish delayed consolidation from immediate excavation loss where groundwater has fallen. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b132-v14-08","title":"體積損失換算：失效診斷","titleEn":"Volume-loss conversion: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「體積損失換算」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Volume-loss conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。","textEn":"Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Combining peak and width from different epochs creates a settlement volume that never actually occurred.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「體積損失換算」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Volume-loss conversion\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。","把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.","Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把毫米當公尺會使體積損失放大千倍，漏掉槽翼又會系統性低估；不同時間的峰值和寬度混用，則會算出未曾存在的沉陷體積。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Confusing millimetres with metres inflates volume loss a thousandfold; omitted flanks underestimate it. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b132-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「穩定基準與閉合」與「差異沉陷與傾斜」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Stable benchmarks and closure\" and \"Differential movement and tilt\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b132-v14-09","title":"穩定基準與閉合：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Stable benchmarks and closure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「穩定基準與閉合」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Stable benchmarks and closure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉陷是相對基準的高程變化，基準點自己移動時整個監測網會出現共同假訊號。基準需位於影響區外且有冗餘連接，水準路線閉合只能檢查內部一致，不能證明全網絕對穩定。 假設觀測點讀得下沉8 mm，基準本身下沉3 mm，真實相對外部穩定基準沉陷為11 mm。 全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「穩定基準與閉合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settlement is elevation change relative to a benchmark. A moving reference creates a common false signal. Redundant external references are required; leveling closure tests internal consistency but does not prove absolute network stability. If an assumed point appears to settle 8 mm relative to a benchmark that itself settles 3 mm, settlement relative to a stable external datum is 11 mm. Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stable benchmarks and closure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「穩定基準與閉合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stable benchmarks and closure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-09-k1","title":"穩定基準與閉合","titleEn":"Stable benchmarks and closure","text":"沉陷是相對基準的高程變化，基準點自己移動時整個監測網會出現共同假訊號。基準需位於影響區外且有冗餘連接，水準路線閉合只能檢查內部一致，不能證明全網絕對穩定。","textEn":"Settlement is elevation change relative to a benchmark. A moving reference creates a common false signal.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「穩定基準與閉合」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Stable benchmarks and closure\" is correct?","options":["沉陷是相對基準的高程變化，基準點自己移動時整個監測網會出現共同假訊號。","水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。","建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Settlement is elevation change relative to a benchmark.","A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.","The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沉陷是相對基準的高程變化，基準點自己移動時整個監測網會出現共同假訊號。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settlement is elevation change relative to a benchmark. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b132-v14-10","title":"穩定基準與閉合：定量估算","titleEn":"Stable benchmarks and closure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「穩定基準與閉合」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Stable benchmarks and closure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設觀測點讀得下沉8 mm，基準本身下沉3 mm，真實相對外部穩定基準沉陷為11 mm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If an assumed point appears to settle 8 mm relative to a benchmark that itself settles 3 mm, settlement relative to a stable external datum is 11 mm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設觀測點讀得下沉8 mm，基準本身下沉3 mm，真實相對外部穩定基準沉陷為11 mm。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. If an assumed point appears to settle 8 mm relative to a benchmark that itself settles 3 mm, settlement relative to a stable external datum is 11 mm.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「穩定基準與閉合」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Stable benchmarks and closure\", which statement holds?","options":["儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。"],"optionsEn":["An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b132-v14-11","title":"穩定基準與閉合：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Stable benchmarks and closure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「穩定基準與閉合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stable benchmarks and closure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄穩定基準與閉合的資料來源與適用條件。閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for stable benchmarks and closure. Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review.","failure":"注意干擾：全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。","textEn":"Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄穩定基準與閉合的資料來源與適用條件。閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for stable benchmarks and closure. Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「穩定基準與閉合」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Stable benchmarks and closure\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。","閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended.","Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"閉合水準網連到多個外部控制點，檢查共同位移模式與獨立GNSS或深層基準證據；基準疑似移動時保留原讀值，經測量主管核准後以可追溯方式重建高程歷程。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Close the leveling network to multiple external controls and compare common movement with independent GNSS or deep benchmarks; preserve raw readings when a reference is suspect and reconstruct elevations traceably under survey-lead review. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b132-v14-12","title":"穩定基準與閉合：失效診斷","titleEn":"Stable benchmarks and closure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「穩定基準與閉合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Stable benchmarks and closure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。","textEn":"Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Trusting internal closure alone silently removes accumulated movement from the risk assessment.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「穩定基準與閉合」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Stable benchmarks and closure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"全網基準同時沉陷可能讓所有監測點看似不動，閉合差仍然很小；若只相信內部閉合，累積沉陷會被悄悄從風險圖中扣掉。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Common settlement of the references can make monitored points appear stationary while closure remains small. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b132-v14-13","title":"差異沉陷與傾斜：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Differential movement and tilt: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「差異沉陷與傾斜」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Differential movement and tilt” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"建物受影響不只看總沉陷，支承間的差異與曲率會誘發結構變形。剛體傾斜與彎曲須分開，因為相同兩點高差可能代表整棟轉動或局部損傷，單一角度不能自動判定損害。 假設兩支點距10 m、高差5 mm，角變化Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000；非通用損害門檻。 只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「差異沉陷與傾斜」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Structural effects depend on differential movement and curvature as well as total settlement. Rigid tilt differs from bending: the same two-point difference may describe whole-building rotation or local distortion, so one angle cannot directly diagnose damage. For assumed support spacing 10 m and differential movement 5 mm, Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000; this is not a universal damage threshold. Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential movement and tilt” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「差異沉陷與傾斜」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Differential movement and tilt”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-13-k1","title":"差異沉陷與傾斜","titleEn":"Differential movement and tilt","text":"建物受影響不只看總沉陷，支承間的差異與曲率會誘發結構變形。剛體傾斜與彎曲須分開，因為相同兩點高差可能代表整棟轉動或局部損傷，單一角度不能自動判定損害。","textEn":"Structural effects depend on differential movement and curvature as well as total settlement. Rigid tilt differs from bending: the same two-point difference may describe whole-building rotation or local distortion, so one angle cannot directly diagnose damage.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「差異沉陷與傾斜」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Differential movement and tilt\" is correct?","options":["建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。","建物受影響不只看總沉陷，支承間的差異與曲率會誘發結構變形。","任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。"],"optionsEn":["The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage.","Structural effects depend on differential movement and curvature as well as total settlement.","Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning."],"answer":1,"explanation":"建物受影響不只看總沉陷，支承間的差異與曲率會誘發結構變形。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Structural effects depend on differential movement and curvature as well as total settlement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b132-v14-14","title":"差異沉陷與傾斜：定量估算","titleEn":"Differential movement and tilt: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「差異沉陷與傾斜」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Differential movement and tilt” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設兩支點距10 m、高差5 mm，角變化Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000；非通用損害門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed support spacing 10 m and differential movement 5 mm, Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000; this is not a universal damage threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設兩支點距10 m、高差5 mm，角變化Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000；非通用損害門檻。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed support spacing 10 m and differential movement 5 mm, Δ/L=0.0005 rad=1/2000; this is not a universal damage threshold.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「差異沉陷與傾斜」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Differential movement and tilt\", which statement holds?","options":["水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。","大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally.","Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b132-v14-15","title":"差異沉陷與傾斜：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Differential movement and tilt: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「差異沉陷與傾斜」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Differential movement and tilt” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄差異沉陷與傾斜的資料來源與適用條件。將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for differential movement and tilt. Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit.","failure":"注意干擾：只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。","textEn":"Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄差異沉陷與傾斜的資料來源與適用條件。將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for differential movement and tilt. Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「差異沉陷與傾斜」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Differential movement and tilt\"?","options":["將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將建物角點水準、傾度與裂縫計同步比較，扣除可識別剛體分量後再檢查曲率；容許值由結構型式、既有缺陷及業主要求決定，不能把教學比值當自動停工標準。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize corner levels, tilt and crack gauges and examine curvature after identifiable rigid-body movement; criteria depend on structure, existing defects and owner requirements, not the teaching ratio as an automatic stop-work limit. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b132-v14-16","title":"差異沉陷與傾斜：失效診斷","titleEn":"Differential movement and tilt: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「差異沉陷與傾斜」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Differential movement and tilt” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。","textEn":"Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Misclassification directs protective measures away from the actual structural load path.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「差異沉陷與傾斜」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Differential movement and tilt\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。","任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending.","Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只看最大沉陷可能忽略短距離高梯度，反之大範圍均勻沉陷也可能被誤判為嚴重彎曲；錯誤分類會讓保護措施沒有針對真正受力路徑。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Maximum settlement alone misses steep local gradients, while broad uniform movement may be mistaken for severe bending. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b132-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「速率與時間窗」與「精度與差值不確定」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Rates and time windows\" and \"Precision of displacement differences\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b132-v14-17","title":"速率與時間窗：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Rates and time windows: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「速率與時間窗」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Rates and time windows” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉陷速率是差分量，時間窗越短越容易放大量測雜訊，越長則可能抹去施工事件。必須把測讀頻率與可能變形速度相配，並將實際時間間隔保留，不能假設所有測次等間距。 假設24 h沉陷增加2 mm，平均速率0.0833 mm/h；若同變化集中在2 h則局部平均1 mm/h。 時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「速率與時間窗」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settlement rate is a difference quotient: short windows amplify noise while long windows obscure events. Sampling must match possible movement speed, retaining actual timestamps rather than assuming equally spaced readings. An assumed 2 mm increase over 24 h averages 0.0833 mm/h; if concentrated within 2 h, the local average is 1 mm/h. Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rates and time windows” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「速率與時間窗」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rates and time windows”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-17-k1","title":"速率與時間窗","titleEn":"Rates and time windows","text":"沉陷速率是差分量，時間窗越短越容易放大量測雜訊，越長則可能抹去施工事件。必須把測讀頻率與可能變形速度相配，並將實際時間間隔保留，不能假設所有測次等間距。","textEn":"Settlement rate is a difference quotient: short windows amplify noise while long windows obscure events. Sampling must match possible movement speed, retaining actual timestamps rather than assuming equally spaced readings.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「速率與時間窗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Rates and time windows\" is correct?","options":["任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。","儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","沉陷速率是差分量，時間窗越短越容易放大量測雜訊，越長則可能抹去施工事件。"],"optionsEn":["Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning.","An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","Settlement rate is a difference quotient: short windows amplify noise while long windows obscure events."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沉陷速率是差分量，時間窗越短越容易放大量測雜訊，越長則可能抹去施工事件。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settlement rate is a difference quotient: short windows amplify noise while long windows obscure events. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b132-v14-18","title":"速率與時間窗：定量估算","titleEn":"Rates and time windows: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「速率與時間窗」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Rates and time windows” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設24 h沉陷增加2 mm，平均速率0.0833 mm/h；若同變化集中在2 h則局部平均1 mm/h。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 mm increase over 24 h averages 0.0833 mm/h; if concentrated within 2 h, the local average is 1 mm/h. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設24 h沉陷增加2 mm，平均速率0.0833 mm/h；若同變化集中在2 h則局部平均1 mm/h。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed 2 mm increase over 24 h averages 0.0833 mm/h; if concentrated within 2 h, the local average is 1 mm/h.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「速率與時間窗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Rates and time windows\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。","掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face.","Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b132-v14-19","title":"速率與時間窗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Rates and time windows: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「速率與時間窗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Rates and time windows” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄速率與時間窗的資料來源與適用條件。並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rates and time windows. Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration.","failure":"注意干擾：時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。","textEn":"Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄速率與時間窗的資料來源與適用條件。並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for rates and time windows. Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「速率與時間窗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Rates and time windows\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。","地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise.","Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"並列原始位移、不同窗長速率與施工事件時間，確認尖峰是否超過儀器噪音；不得平滑後刪除異常，監測負責人應先核對測點狀況，再依核准應變計畫處理持續加速。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Display raw movement, rates from several windows and construction timestamps, checking peaks against noise; do not erase anomalies through smoothing, and verify point condition before applying the approved response plan to sustained acceleration. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b132-v14-20","title":"速率與時間窗：失效診斷","titleEn":"Rates and time windows: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「速率與時間窗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rates and time windows” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。","textEn":"Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Reviewing rate and accumulated displacement together is necessary to identify these opposite risks.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「速率與時間窗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Rates and time windows\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement."],"answer":2,"explanation":"時間戳錯誤或漏測可產生假加速度，過長平均又會讓急遽變形延後被發現；將速率與累積量分開審查才能辨識兩種相反風險。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Incorrect timestamps or missed observations create false acceleration, while excessive averaging delays recognition of rapid movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b132-v14-21","title":"精度與差值不確定：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Precision of displacement differences: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「精度與差值不確定」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Precision of displacement differences” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"兩次高程相減會累積各測次不確定性，若共享同一儀器校準，誤差還可能相關。解析度只是最小顯示增量，不等於可辨識沉陷；判斷微小變化時需有重複測量與環境補償。 假設兩次高程各標準不確定0.5 mm且獨立，差值u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm。 以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「精度與差值不確定」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Differencing elevations combines epoch uncertainties, which may correlate through shared calibration. Resolution is only display increment, not detectable settlement. Small changes require repeat observations and environmental checks before interpretation. Assuming independent elevation standard uncertainties of 0.5 mm at each epoch, the difference has u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm. Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Precision of displacement differences” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「精度與差值不確定」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Precision of displacement differences”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-21-k1","title":"精度與差值不確定","titleEn":"Precision of displacement differences","text":"兩次高程相減會累積各測次不確定性，若共享同一儀器校準，誤差還可能相關。解析度只是最小顯示增量，不等於可辨識沉陷；判斷微小變化時需有重複測量與環境補償。","textEn":"Differencing elevations combines epoch uncertainties, which may correlate through shared calibration. Resolution is only display increment, not detectable settlement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「精度與差值不確定」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Precision of displacement differences\" is correct?","options":["兩次高程相減會累積各測次不確定性，若共享同一儀器校準，誤差還可能相關。","儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。"],"optionsEn":["Differencing elevations combines epoch uncertainties, which may correlate through shared calibration.","An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩次高程相減會累積各測次不確定性，若共享同一儀器校準，誤差還可能相關。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Differencing elevations combines epoch uncertainties, which may correlate through shared calibration. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b132-v14-22","title":"精度與差值不確定：定量估算","titleEn":"Precision of displacement differences: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「精度與差值不確定」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Precision of displacement differences” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設兩次高程各標準不確定0.5 mm且獨立，差值u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assuming independent elevation standard uncertainties of 0.5 mm at each epoch, the difference has u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設兩次高程各標準不確定0.5 mm且獨立，差值u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assuming independent elevation standard uncertainties of 0.5 mm at each epoch, the difference has u=√(0.5²+0.5²)=0.707 mm.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「精度與差值不確定」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Precision of displacement differences\", which statement holds?","options":["大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b132-v14-23","title":"精度與差值不確定：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Precision of displacement differences: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「精度與差值不確定」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Precision of displacement differences” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄精度與差值不確定的資料來源與適用條件。以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for precision of displacement differences. Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead.","failure":"注意干擾：以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。","textEn":"Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄精度與差值不確定的資料來源與適用條件。以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for precision of displacement differences. Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「精度與差值不確定」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Precision of displacement differences\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。","以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.","Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以穩定控制點重複觀測估計實際散布，分離儀器、立尺與環境貢獻；對小於可辨識程度的變化標記不確定，而不是強制畫成平順趨勢，並由測量主管核准資料品質旗標。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate field scatter from repeated stable controls and separate instrument, staff and environmental contributions; flag unresolved small changes instead of forcing a smooth trend, with quality flags approved by the survey lead. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b132-v14-24","title":"精度與差值不確定：失效診斷","titleEn":"Precision of displacement differences: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「精度與差值不確定」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Precision of displacement differences” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。","textEn":"Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Repeated false alerts can weaken the response to genuine abnormal movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「精度與差值不確定」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Precision of displacement differences\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。"],"optionsEn":["Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以0.1 mm顯示位數宣稱0.1 mm準確度會過度解讀噪音，若只挑單次最大變化又會製造假警報；反覆誤報可能削弱團隊對真異常的反應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Claiming 0.1 mm accuracy from display resolution overinterprets noise, while choosing the largest single difference creates false alarms. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b132-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「地下水下降與固結」與「施工里程與多源事件」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Drawdown and consolidation\" and \"Chainage and multiple events\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b132-v14-25","title":"地下水下降與固結：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Drawdown and consolidation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「地下水下降與固結」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Drawdown and consolidation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水位降低可增加有效應力並引發延時固結，影響範圍未必與即時沉陷槽相同。必須分開孔壓下降與總應力變化，水位穿越土層改變單位重時，簡單γwΔh換算不能直接完整代表。 假設總應力不變且測點孔壓降低γwΔh，水頭降2 m使Δσ′=9.81×2=19.62 kPa；總重改變須另算。 把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「地下水下降與固結」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Drawdown may increase effective stress and cause delayed consolidation beyond the immediate trough. Separate pore-pressure reduction from changing total stress; when a water table crosses layers and changes unit weight, γwΔh alone is incomplete. Assume total stress remains fixed and point pore pressure falls by γwΔh; a 2 m head drop gives Δσ′=19.62 kPa, requiring separate treatment if total weight changes. Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drawdown and consolidation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「地下水下降與固結」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drawdown and consolidation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-25-k1","title":"地下水下降與固結","titleEn":"Drawdown and consolidation","text":"水位降低可增加有效應力並引發延時固結，影響範圍未必與即時沉陷槽相同。必須分開孔壓下降與總應力變化，水位穿越土層改變單位重時，簡單γwΔh換算不能直接完整代表。","textEn":"Drawdown may increase effective stress and cause delayed consolidation beyond the immediate trough. Separate pore-pressure reduction from changing total stress; when a water table crosses layers and changes unit weight, γwΔh alone is incomplete.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「地下水下降與固結」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Drawdown and consolidation\" is correct?","options":["水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。","水位降低可增加有效應力並引發延時固結，影響範圍未必與即時沉陷槽相同。","每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。"],"optionsEn":["Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally.","Drawdown may increase effective stress and cause delayed consolidation beyond the immediate trough.","Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face."],"answer":1,"explanation":"水位降低可增加有效應力並引發延時固結，影響範圍未必與即時沉陷槽相同。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Drawdown may increase effective stress and cause delayed consolidation beyond the immediate trough. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b132-v14-26","title":"地下水下降與固結：定量估算","titleEn":"Drawdown and consolidation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「地下水下降與固結」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Drawdown and consolidation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設總應力不變且測點孔壓降低γwΔh，水頭降2 m使Δσ′=9.81×2=19.62 kPa；總重改變須另算。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume total stress remains fixed and point pore pressure falls by γwΔh; a 2 m head drop gives Δσ′=19.62 kPa, requiring separate treatment if total weight changes. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設總應力不變且測點孔壓降低γwΔh，水頭降2 m使Δσ′=9.81×2=19.62 kPa；總重改變須另算。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assume total stress remains fixed and point pore pressure falls by γwΔh; a 2 m head drop gives Δσ′=19.62 kPa, requiring separate treatment if total weight changes.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「地下水下降與固結」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Drawdown and consolidation\", which statement holds?","options":["掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。","地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended.","Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b132-v14-27","title":"地下水下降與固結：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Drawdown and consolidation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「地下水下降與固結」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drawdown and consolidation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄地下水下降與固結的資料來源與適用條件。將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for drawdown and consolidation. Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone.","failure":"注意干擾：把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。","textEn":"Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄地下水下降與固結的資料來源與適用條件。將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for drawdown and consolidation. Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「地下水下降與固結」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Drawdown and consolidation\"?","options":["將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將多深度孔壓、地表沉陷與抽排水量同步，檢查沉陷是否在開挖通過後仍持續；以壓縮性試驗與排水邊界分析時間尺度，不能只憑兩條相似曲線宣稱因果。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Synchronize multilevel pore pressure, settlement and pumping, checking whether movement persists after passage; use compressibility tests and drainage boundaries to assess timescale rather than inferring causality from two similar curves alone. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b132-v14-28","title":"地下水下降與固結：失效診斷","titleEn":"Drawdown and consolidation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「地下水下降與固結」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drawdown and consolidation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。","textEn":"Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Hydraulic and construction evidence are needed together.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「地下水下降與固結」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Drawdown and consolidation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。","每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action.","Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把延時固結全歸為潛盾出土過多會選錯控制手段，反之將局部失土都當地下水效應又可能延誤處置；需要水文與施工證據共同辨識。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing all consolidation to excess muck removal selects the wrong control, while blaming localized ground loss on groundwater can delay action. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b132-v14-29","title":"施工里程與多源事件：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Chainage and multiple events: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「施工里程與多源事件」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Chainage and multiple events” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"同一監測點可能受雙線隧道、車站開挖、灌漿與外部施工影響，位移對時間曲線需要連到各事件位置。將所有變化歸給最近掌子面會忽略延時與重疊，應建立可比較的事件索引。 假設掌子面距測點30 m、隧道直徑6 m，規一化距離x/D=5；兩條線比較需同樣定義正負方向。 錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「施工里程與多源事件」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A point may respond to twin drives, station excavation, grouting and unrelated works. Time histories must connect to each event location. Assigning every change to the nearest face ignores delay and overlap, requiring a comparable event index. For assumed face distance 30 m and diameter 6 m, normalized distance x/D=5; comparing drives requires the same sign convention. Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Chainage and multiple events” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「施工里程與多源事件」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Chainage and multiple events”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-29-k1","title":"施工里程與多源事件","titleEn":"Chainage and multiple events","text":"同一監測點可能受雙線隧道、車站開挖、灌漿與外部施工影響，位移對時間曲線需要連到各事件位置。將所有變化歸給最近掌子面會忽略延時與重疊，應建立可比較的事件索引。","textEn":"A point may respond to twin drives, station excavation, grouting and unrelated works. Time histories must connect to each event location.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「施工里程與多源事件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Chainage and multiple events\" is correct?","options":["每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。","大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。","同一監測點可能受雙線隧道、車站開挖、灌漿與外部施工影響，位移對時間曲線需要連到各事件位置。"],"optionsEn":["Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face.","Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.","A point may respond to twin drives, station excavation, grouting and unrelated works."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一監測點可能受雙線隧道、車站開挖、灌漿與外部施工影響，位移對時間曲線需要連到各事件位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A point may respond to twin drives, station excavation, grouting and unrelated works. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b132-v14-30","title":"施工里程與多源事件：定量估算","titleEn":"Chainage and multiple events: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「施工里程與多源事件」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Chainage and multiple events” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設掌子面距測點30 m、隧道直徑6 m，規一化距離x/D=5；兩條線比較需同樣定義正負方向。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed face distance 30 m and diameter 6 m, normalized distance x/D=5; comparing drives requires the same sign convention. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設掌子面距測點30 m、隧道直徑6 m，規一化距離x/D=5；兩條線比較需同樣定義正負方向。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. For assumed face distance 30 m and diameter 6 m, normalized distance x/D=5; comparing drives requires the same sign convention.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「施工里程與多源事件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Chainage and multiple events\", which statement holds?","options":["以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。","水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。"],"optionsEn":["The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width.","A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b132-v14-31","title":"施工里程與多源事件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Chainage and multiple events: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「施工里程與多源事件」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Chainage and multiple events” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄施工里程與多源事件的資料來源與適用條件。把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for chainage and multiple events. Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence.","failure":"注意干擾：錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。","textEn":"Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄施工里程與多源事件的資料來源與適用條件。把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for chainage and multiple events. Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「施工里程與多源事件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Chainage and multiple events\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。","任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs.","Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把位移同時對時間與規一化掌子面距離作圖，加入灌漿及抽水日誌；多事件重疊時比較未受同一事件影響的控制點，地工主管需列出可能成因及可區分它們的證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Plot movement against both time and normalized face distance, including grouting and pumping logs; use suitable control points during overlapping events and require the geotechnical lead to list competing causes and distinguishing evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b132-v14-32","title":"施工里程與多源事件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Chainage and multiple events: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「施工里程與多源事件」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Chainage and multiple events” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「每個監測點的變形只能由距離最近的掌子面造成。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Movement at a monitoring point can only be caused by the nearest face.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。","textEn":"Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「施工里程與多源事件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Chainage and multiple events\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。","錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.","Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages."],"answer":2,"explanation":"錯誤時區或機器里程會將沉陷峰錯配施工階段，雙線效果重疊又可能被誤當第二條線單獨造成；這會扭曲事後經驗參數與責任判斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Wrong time zones or machine chainage misassign settlement peaks to stages; overlapping twin-drive effects can be attributed entirely to the second drive, biasing empirical parameters and retrospective responsibility assessments. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b132-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「警戒邏輯與量測確認」與「長期追蹤與結案」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation\" and \"Long-term tracking and closeout\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b132-v14-33","title":"警戒邏輯與量測確認：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「警戒邏輯與量測確認」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"警戒值應連到可執行的回應與量測確認流程，而非只有紅黃綠色。位移、速率與結構症狀提供不同證據，持續超限和單點跳值需分辨，但不能以資料確認為由延誤已核准的緊急回應。 假設教學警戒比r=量測8 mm/審查值10 mm=0.8；此10 mm純為算例，現場需個案核准。 只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「警戒邏輯與量測確認」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Triggers require actionable responses and measurement confirmation, not only colors. Displacement, rate and structural symptoms provide different evidence; distinguish persistent exceedance from isolated jumps without delaying an approved emergency response. An assumed teaching trigger ratio is measured 8 mm/review value 10 mm=0.8; the 10 mm value is purely illustrative and requires project-specific approval in practice. Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「警戒邏輯與量測確認」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-33-k1","title":"警戒邏輯與量測確認","titleEn":"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation","text":"警戒值應連到可執行的回應與量測確認流程，而非只有紅黃綠色。位移、速率與結構症狀提供不同證據，持續超限和單點跳值需分辨，但不能以資料確認為由延誤已核准的緊急回應。","textEn":"Triggers require actionable responses and measurement confirmation, not only colors. Displacement, rate and structural symptoms provide different evidence; distinguish persistent exceedance from isolated jumps without delaying an approved emergency response.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「警戒邏輯與量測確認」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation\" is correct?","options":["警戒值應連到可執行的回應與量測確認流程，而非只有紅黃綠色。","大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。","掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。"],"optionsEn":["Triggers require actionable responses and measurement confirmation, not only colors.","Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.","Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended."],"answer":0,"explanation":"警戒值應連到可執行的回應與量測確認流程，而非只有紅黃綠色。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Triggers require actionable responses and measurement confirmation, not only colors. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b132-v14-34","title":"警戒邏輯與量測確認：定量估算","titleEn":"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「警戒邏輯與量測確認」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設教學警戒比r=量測8 mm/審查值10 mm=0.8；此10 mm純為算例，現場需個案核准。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed teaching trigger ratio is measured 8 mm/review value 10 mm=0.8; the 10 mm value is purely illustrative and requires project-specific approval in practice. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設教學警戒比r=量測8 mm/審查值10 mm=0.8；此10 mm純為算例，現場需個案核准。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. An assumed teaching trigger ratio is measured 8 mm/review value 10 mm=0.8; the 10 mm value is purely illustrative and requires project-specific approval in practice.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「警戒邏輯與量測確認」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation\", which statement holds?","options":["地表體積損失百分比就是直接量得的超挖土量百分比。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","建物總沉陷最大時，一定也承受最大的彎曲損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Surface volume-loss percentage is a directly measured overexcavation percentage.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","The building with the largest total settlement necessarily suffers the most bending damage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b132-v14-35","title":"警戒邏輯與量測確認：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「警戒邏輯與量測確認」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄警戒邏輯與量測確認的資料來源與適用條件。用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for trigger logic and measurement confirmation. Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table.","failure":"注意干擾：只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。","textEn":"Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄警戒邏輯與量測確認的資料來源與適用條件。用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for trigger logic and measurement confirmation. Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「警戒邏輯與量測確認」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","儀器顯示到十分之一毫米就具有同等實際準確度。","用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","An instrument displaying tenths of a millimetre has the same actual accuracy.","Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用模擬資料演練超限通知、備援讀值與責任人接收，確認通訊斷線也會被標示；工程師審查門檻的依據、延遲與可採行措施，不能把本課比值部署成現場控制表。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Rehearse notification, backup readings and acknowledgment with synthetic data, including communication loss; engineers review criteria, latency and feasible actions, and the teaching ratio must not be deployed as a field control table. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b132-v14-36","title":"警戒邏輯與量測確認：失效診斷","titleEn":"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「警戒邏輯與量測確認」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Trigger logic and measurement confirmation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「大部分監測點正常就能取消少數敏感建物的超限警報。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normal readings at most points justify canceling an exceedance at a sensitive building.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。","textEn":"Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Without a named recipient, technically correct detection may still fail to produce a response.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「警戒邏輯與量測確認」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Trigger logic and measurement confirmation\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。"],"optionsEn":["Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended."],"answer":0,"explanation":"只依平均值判斷可能掩蓋單一敏感建物，儀器斷線被當成零位移更危險；若警報沒有指定接收者，即使系統正確偵測也未必產生回應。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Averages can hide one sensitive building, and treating lost communication as zero movement is worse. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b132-v14-37","title":"長期追蹤與結案：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Long-term tracking and closeout: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「長期追蹤與結案」如何影響隧道地表沉陷監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Long-term tracking and closeout” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Surface-settlement monitoring for tunneling”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"施工通過不代表所有沉陷立即停止，黏土固結及地下水恢復可能延續。結案需有基準穩定、速率趨勢和建物狀況的共同證據，並保留後續營運期能銜接的坐標與時間基準。 假設連續四週增量0.8、0.4、0.2、0.1 mm，總增量1.5 mm；遞減趨勢不等於未來必定為零。 過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「長期追蹤與結案」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Passage does not end settlement immediately; clay consolidation and groundwater recovery can continue. Closeout needs stable references, rate trends and asset condition together, preserving coordinates and time datums for operational monitoring. Assumed weekly increments 0.8,0.4,0.2 and 0.1 mm total 1.5 mm; a decreasing trend does not prove zero future movement. Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long-term tracking and closeout” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings.","failure":"常見誤解：「掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「長期追蹤與結案」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Long-term tracking and closeout”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-37-k1","title":"長期追蹤與結案","titleEn":"Long-term tracking and closeout","text":"施工通過不代表所有沉陷立即停止，黏土固結及地下水恢復可能延續。結案需有基準穩定、速率趨勢和建物狀況的共同證據，並保留後續營運期能銜接的坐標與時間基準。","textEn":"Passage does not end settlement immediately; clay consolidation and groundwater recovery can continue. Closeout needs stable references, rate trends and asset condition together, preserving coordinates and time datums for operational monitoring.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「長期追蹤與結案」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Long-term tracking and closeout\" is correct?","options":["掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。","施工通過不代表所有沉陷立即停止，黏土固結及地下水恢復可能延續。","量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended.","Passage does not end settlement immediately; clay consolidation and groundwater recovery can continue.","The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"施工通過不代表所有沉陷立即停止，黏土固結及地下水恢復可能延續。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Passage does not end settlement immediately; clay consolidation and groundwater recovery can continue. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b132-v14-38","title":"長期追蹤與結案：定量估算","titleEn":"Long-term tracking and closeout: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「長期追蹤與結案」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Long-term tracking and closeout” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設連續四週增量0.8、0.4、0.2、0.1 mm，總增量1.5 mm；遞減趨勢不等於未來必定為零。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed weekly increments 0.8,0.4,0.2 and 0.1 mm total 1.5 mm; a decreasing trend does not prove zero future movement. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。假設連續四週增量0.8、0.4、0.2、0.1 mm，總增量1.5 mm；遞減趨勢不等於未來必定為零。","textEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Assumed weekly increments 0.8,0.4,0.2 and 0.1 mm total 1.5 mm; a decreasing trend does not prove zero future movement.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「長期追蹤與結案」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Long-term tracking and closeout\", which statement holds?","options":["水準網閉合差很小，就證明所有基準點絕對穩定。","任何時間窗算出的平均沉陷速率都有相同工程意義。","以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。"],"optionsEn":["A small leveling closure proves absolute stability of every benchmark.","Average settlement rates from any time window have the same engineering meaning.","The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以下為教學假設，非現場操作設定。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"The following are teaching assumptions, not field operating settings. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b132-v14-39","title":"長期追蹤與結案：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Long-term tracking and closeout: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長期追蹤與結案」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Long-term tracking and closeout” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時逐項記錄長期追蹤與結案的資料來源與適用條件。以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for long-term tracking and closeout. Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions.","failure":"注意干擾：過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。驗證亦須釐清下列替代解釋：過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。","textEn":"Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions. Verification must also resolve this competing explanation: Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時逐項記錄長期追蹤與結案的資料來源與適用條件。以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。","textEn":"At handover, document the evidence and applicable conditions for long-term tracking and closeout. Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「長期追蹤與結案」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Long-term tracking and closeout\"?","options":["以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","水位下降時總應力永遠不變，可以無條件使用水頭換算。"],"optionsEn":["Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Total stress never changes during drawdown, so head conversion applies unconditionally."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以固定方法檢查長期讀值、孔壓恢復和既有裂縫，說明監測停止或降頻的個案依據；交付原始資料、校正歷程與未解決項，由業主及工程負責人共同確認接管條件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Review long-term levels, pressure recovery and existing cracks consistently, justifying any reduced frequency or cessation; deliver raw data, corrections and unresolved issues for joint owner and engineering approval of handover conditions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b132-v14-40","title":"長期追蹤與結案：失效診斷","titleEn":"Long-term tracking and closeout: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"prerequisiteIds":["b132-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「長期追蹤與結案」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long-term tracking and closeout” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「掌子面通過後就可以立刻認定延時沉陷已經結束。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Face passage immediately establishes that all delayed settlement has ended.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b132-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。","textEn":"Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Unstated residual uncertainty can lead an operator to assume that permanent stability has been demonstrated.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]},{"id":"b132-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「長期追蹤與結案」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Long-term tracking and closeout\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。","量到沉陷槽中央最大值就能唯一決定槽的寬度。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history.","The maximum centerline settlement uniquely determines the trough width."],"answer":1,"explanation":"過早拆除基準會切斷延時沉陷的證據鏈，若只交最後讀值則無法追查速率；未明示剩餘不確定性，營運者可能誤以為已證實永久穩定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Removing benchmarks prematurely breaks evidence for delayed movement, while final readings alone lose rate history. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-stepney-settlement","v14s-crossrail-monitoring","v14s-fhwa","v14s-crossrail-geology","v7-gotthard-network"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
